### MEDIUM: Test Logic Issue — Non-Owner Access Test

**File: `packages/testing/playwright/tests/ui/18-user-management.spec.ts:22-27`**

```typescript
test('should prevent non-owners to access UM settings', async ({ n8n }) => {
    await n8n.api.users.create();  // Creates user AND logs in as them (shared cookies)
    await n8n.navigate.toUsers();
    await expect(n8n.workflows.getProjectName()).toBeVisible();
});
```

`api.users.create()` uses the shared `api` fixture which **sets cookies on the current context**. After this call, `n8n` is authenticated as the new user (not the owner). The test then navigates to `/settings/users` and expects to see the project name (implying redirect to home). But it doesn't assert the URL changed or that access was denied — just that a workflow element is visible. A false positive if the new user *can* access the page.

---

